1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,018
Inkanyamba: whoever he used to be no longer matters.

2
00:00:03,018 --> 00:00:05,057
He has become a creature of pure wrath.

3
00:00:05,277 --> 00:00:06,557
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:11,172
Put the Killer Wrath card out with a tracking marker on level two, and add both

5
00:00:11,172 --> 00:00:13,340
Atonement Action cards to the Action Tableau.

6
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:18,354
Killer Wrath is his rising anger. Increase and Decrease move the marker, always

7
00:00:18,354 --> 00:00:19,415
between one and ten.

8
00:00:19,635 --> 00:00:23,627
Unleash means apply the current level, which can raise Horror, heal him, make him

9
00:00:23,627 --> 00:00:25,352
take a Killer Action, or all three.

10
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:30,475
Atonement cards are your main way to lower his Wrath, or Divine Wrath at the Sacred

11
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:30,839
Groves.

12
00:00:31,059 --> 00:00:34,600
They have an extra success line for three or more successes on a Horror roll.

13
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:39,160
Wrath of Death raises his Wrath by your current health, so being at full health

14
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:39,679
hurts here.

15
00:00:39,899 --> 00:00:44,099
Volatile Temper adds a Horror roll at the end of each Upkeep that can Unleash him,

16
00:00:44,099 --> 00:00:47,685
and Dark Lightning kills a second Victim nearby whenever he kills one.

17
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:52,780
A few tips. At the Sacred Groves two Wrath tracks stack, and it's the hardest box in

18
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:54,665
the game, so try him elsewhere first.

19
00:00:54,885 --> 00:00:59,579
Atonement is unreliable on one or two dice, so get Horror down first and roll three.

20
00:00:59,799 --> 00:01:02,722
Look for weapons that hurt him and lower Wrath at once.

21
00:01:02,722 --> 00:01:05,326
And beware Savage Whirlwind, his toughest Finale.

22
00:01:05,326 --> 00:01:05,857
Good luck.

